.TH PE_HEADER 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
pe_header, pe_header_nt, pe_header_sig, pe_header_nt32, pe_header_nt64, pe_header_coff, pe_header_opt, pe_header_opt32, pe_header_opt64, pe_header_sections, pe_header_datadir \- Retrieve headers and directories from a Portable Executable (PE) file

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/pe.h>
.IB #include <lib/uint16.h>

.IB void*
.IB pe_header_nt(void* pe);

.IB uint32
.IB pe_header_sig(void* pe);

.IB pe32_nt_headers*
.IB pe_header_nt32(void* pe);

.IB pe64_nt_headers*
.IB pe_header_nt64(void* pe);

.IB pe_coff_header*
.IB pe_header_coff(void* pe);

.IB void*
.IB pe_header_opt(void* pe);

.IB pe32_opt_header*
.IB pe_header_opt32(void* pe);

.IB pe64_opt_header*
.IB pe_header_opt64(void* pe);

.IB pe_section_header*
.IB pe_header_sections(void* pe, uint16* nsections);

.IB pe_data_directory*
.IB pe_header_datadir(void* pe);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBpe_header\fR family of functions retrieves various headers and directories from a Portable Executable (PE) file. These functions help in accessing the different parts of a PE file's structure, such as the DOS header, NT headers, COFF header, optional header, and section headers.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.IB pe
The pointer to the PE file.

.SH RETURN VALUES
.TP
.IB pe_header_nt
Returns a pointer to the NT headers.
.TP
.IB pe_header_sig
Returns the signature of the PE file.
.TP
.IB pe_header_nt32
Returns a pointer to the 32-bit NT headers if the PE file is 32-bit, otherwise returns NULL.
.TP
.IB pe_header_nt64
Returns a pointer to the 64-bit NT headers if the PE file is 64-bit, otherwise returns NULL.
.TP
.IB pe_header_coff
Returns a pointer to the COFF header.
.TP
.IB pe_header_opt
Returns a pointer to the optional header.
.TP
.IB pe_header_opt32
Returns a pointer to the 32-bit optional header if the PE file is 32-bit, otherwise returns NULL.
.TP
.IB pe_header_opt64
Returns a pointer to the 64-bit optional header if the PE file is 64-bit, otherwise returns NULL.
.TP
.IB pe_header_sections
Returns a pointer to the section headers and sets the number of sections if \fInsections\fR is not NULL.
.TP
.IB pe_header_datadir
Returns a pointer to the data directories.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBpe_header\fR functions:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/pe.h>
#include <lib/uint16.h>

int main() {
    uint8 pe_data[1024];
    void* pe = pe_data;
    uint32 sig = pe_header_sig(pe);
    if (sig == 0x45504544) {  // "PE\0\0"
        pe32_nt_headers* nt32 = pe_header_nt32(pe);
        if (nt32) {
            printf("PE file is 32-bit\n");
            printf("Machine: %u\n", nt32->machine);
            printf("Number of Sections: %u\n", nt32->number_of_sections);
            printf("Optional Header Size: %u\n", nt32->size_of_optional_header);
        }
    }
    return 0;
}
.nef

